      "targeted_symptom": "S033",
      "patient_response": "My mood? Oh, um... well, I hope this doesn't make me sound awful. I try so hard to be a good person, especially for the folks I look after at work. \n\nIt's just been a little... up and down, I suppose? Sometimes I feel just so... bright and chosen, if that makes sense. Like I have all these wonderful ideas and the whole town of Greenville just can't even hold all my plans. It's actually a really nice feeling, I hope it's alright that I get like that. \n\nBut then... and I'm so embarrassed to admit this to you... sometimes I get really short. I'll go from feeling just on top of the world to... well, to snapping hard at someone over the littlest thing. Like, if one of my clients just asks me to repeat myself, I'll just snap at them. I always feel so guilty right after, because I know they can't help it, and I promise you I'm really not a mean person at heart. \n\nAm I explaining that okay? I just want to make sure I'm giving you the right answers.",
